Package: universal-downloader
Version: 2.0.5
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Universal Downloader <packaging@universal-downloader.local>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-pyqt6, xdg-utils
Recommends: yt-dlp, aria2, curl, ffmpeg, libnotify-bin
Description: Lightweight gaming-styled download manager for Linux
 Universal Downloader is a graphical desktop application for downloading
 videos and files from YouTube (yt-dlp), Google Drive (gdown), MEGA
 (MEGAcmd) and direct file links (aria2c). It offers a persistent queue,
 real progress read from the download tools, resume and retry, download
 history and settings, and is designed to stay responsive on low-end
 hardware such as a 4 GB RAM, dual-core computer running Linux Mint XFCE.
 .
 No Electron, no Chromium and no bundled binaries: it is a native Python
 PyQt6 program that calls the system's download tools. Missing tools are
 detected and explained in-app (Dependency doctor) instead of failing
 silently.
 .
 Note: gdown and MEGAcmd are not in the Mint/Ubuntu package archive; the
 application detects them at runtime and tells you how to install them.
Homepage: https://github.com/mudasarashraf1998/Mads_experiment
